# PinHunt API server and staging tools — STAGING. Copy to .env.staging
# (gitignored) and fill in. Nothing here is a production secret: production is
# identified by its ref and pooler host only, and its password is typed at a
# prompt when you export the schema.
#
# Every script that writes to a database refuses to run unless all of these
# identify a prepared staging project (scripts/lib/staging-guard.mjs).
PINHUNT_ENV=staging
STAGING_PROJECT_REF=<staging-project-ref>
PRODUCTION_PROJECT_REF=<production-project-ref>

# Dashboard → Connect → Session pooler → host (e.g. aws-1-eu-west-1.pooler.supabase.com).
STAGING_DB_HOST=<staging-session-pooler-host>
PRODUCTION_DB_HOST=<production-session-pooler-host>
# Where schema exports go. Must be outside every git repository.
STAGING_EXPORT_DIR=~/PinHunt-Private/staging

SUPABASE_URL=https://<staging-project-ref>.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<staging-anon-key>
# Staging service-role key. Server-side only; never in the app or in git.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<staging-service-role-key>

PORT=3000
LOG_LEVEL=info
NODE_ENV=development

# ── Paid APIs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave blank to keep staging free: scan, Vision and Pixian features then fail
# with their normal "not configured" errors. For scan tests, use a separate
# OpenAI project key with a low monthly budget, not the production key.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Leave OPENAI_SCAN_MODEL unset: an empty value overrides the default model.
# OPENAI_SCAN_MODEL=
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS_JSON=
PIXIAN_API_ID=
PIXIAN_API_SECRET=
# true = free watermarked Pixian results. Keep true in staging.
PIXIAN_TEST_MODE=true

# eBay valuation: sandbox keys only in staging.
EBAY_CLIENT_ID=
EBAY_CLIENT_SECRET=
EBAY_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox
